{"id":"0224cec8e2295cc4b6a43cdd404e3e541b77c6f4","axis":"silent","repo":"salvo-rs/salvo","sha":"0224cec8e2295cc4b6a43cdd404e3e541b77c6f4","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md","lines":["@@ -45,18 +45,25 @@ substitute the narrower consumer for the root or RustCrypto feature graph."," "," ## RustCrypto JWT: RUSTSEC-2026-0387"," ","-The fresh root lockfile still contains `jsonwebtoken 11.1.0 -> p256/p384 0.13 ->","-elliptic-curve 0.13.8 -> crypto-bigint 0.5.5`. The patched crypto-bigint range is","-`>=0.7.6`, which does not satisfy this upstream requirement. Salvo enables this","-JWT backend through `salvo-jwt-auth/ring` or `salvo/jwt-auth-ring`; the separate","-`salvo/ring` feature selects TLS crypto only. Cargo features are additive, so","-choosing AWS-LC at runtime does not remove an enabled RustCrypto dependency.","-","-Owner: Salvo maintainers. Recheck on upstream jsonwebtoken/RustCrypto releases","-and before publishing a dependency refresh. Upgrade a supported upstream graph,","-then audit all affected feature configurations. There is no exception for this","-finding. It concerns secret-integer operations; its presence does not by itself","-prove a timing attack on public-key token verification.","+The workspace now requires jsonwebtoken 12. Its RustCrypto backend uses","+`p256/p384 0.14 -> elliptic-curve 0.14 -> crypto-bigint 0.7`, and RSA uses the","+0.10 family. A fresh root resolution on 2026-11-15 selected crypto-bigint","+0.7.11 and rsa 0.10.0 for JWT, removing the crypto-bigint 0.5 path reported in","+the dated 2026-11-09 snapshot above. cargo-audit against RustSec DB","+`02e2517f457a359fc6d3440ea4560c8ea188fee8` reported no findings under the existing","+RSA exception below. No new advisory exception was added.","+","+The patched crypto-bigint range is `>=0.7.6`. Refresh and audit application","+lockfiles rather than assuming a compatible version range guarantees a patched","+resolution. Salvo's `salvo-jwt-auth/ring` and `salvo/jwt-auth-ring` features select","+the RustCrypto JWT backend; the separate `salvo/ring` feature selects TLS crypto.","+Cargo features are additive, so choosing AWS-LC at runtime does not remove an","+enabled RustCrypto dependency. Both JWT providers and their combined feature","+configuration are tested.","+","+`ConstDecoder::from_secret`, `DecodingKey::from_secret`, and","+`EncodingKey::from_secret` now return `Result` and reject empty HMAC secrets.","+Handle constructor errors during application configuration when upgrading."," [Advisory](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0387.html)."," "," ## RSA exception: RUSTSEC-2023-0071"],"additions":19,"deletions":12,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/security-audits/2026-11-15-jwt12.json","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@","+{","+  \"date\": \"2026-11-15\",","+  \"source_base\": \"e8128e21bd54ba737300f39754ab8160b607074a\",","+  \"change\": \"Upgrade root and examples JWT to jsonwebtoken 12\",","+  \"scope\": \"root workspace, including optional RustCrypto JWT dependencies\",","+  \"command\": \"cargo generate-lockfile; cargo audit --json\",","+  \"toolchain\": \"rustc 1.99.1 (58cf8f9c3 2026-10-13)\",","+  \"cargo_audit\": \"0.22.0\",","+  \"lockfile_sha256\": \"478ce1b8f78448c5d9fdf8563266b2ad97e42053bab1b8e4875a6576f317fc10\",","+  \"database\": {","+    \"advisory-count\": 1509,","+    \"last-commit\": \"02e2517f457a359fc6d3440ea4560c8ea188fee8\",","+    \"last-updated\": \"2026-11-15T10:59:21+01:00\"","+  },","+  \"outcome\": \"clean\",","+  \"vulnerabilities\": [],","+  \"warnings\": {},","+  \"existing_ignored_advisories\": [","+    \"RUSTSEC-2023-0071\"","+  ],","+  \"resolved_versions\": [","+    {","+      \"name\": \"crypto-bigint\",","+      \"version\": \"0.7.11\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"name\": \"elliptic-curve\",","+      \"version\": \"0.14.3\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"name\": \"jsonwebtoken\",","+      \"version\": \"12.0.0\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"name\": \"p256\",","+      \"version\": \"0.14.0\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"name\": \"p384\",","+      \"version\": \"0.14.0\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"name\": \"rsa\",","+      \"version\": \"0.9.10\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"name\": \"rsa\",","+      \"version\": \"0.10.0\"","+    }","+  ],","+  \"notes\": [","+    \"The existing RSA exception still applies to certon 0.4 -> rsa 0.9; this JWT change does not remove or broaden it.\",","+    \"This is a dated resolution; refresh application lockfiles and audit them.\",","+    \"Raw-secret constructors are fallible in jsonwebtoken 12 and reject empty keys.\"","+  ]","+}"],"additions":56,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ hyper-rustls = { version = \"0.27\", default-features = false }"," hyper-util = { version = \"0.1\", default-features = true }"," indexmap = \"2\""," inventory = \"0.3\"","-jsonwebtoken = \"11\"","+jsonwebtoken = \"12\""," local-ip-address = \"0.6\""," mime = \"0.3\""," mime-infer = \"4\""],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/jwt-auth/README.md","lines":["@@ -75,14 +75,10 @@ RustCrypto provider for JWTs instead, disable Salvo's default features and"," select `jwt-auth-ring`. The separate `ring` feature selects ring for Salvo's"," rustls integration:"," ","-**Current dependency limitation:** the RustCrypto JWT backend selected by","-`jwt-auth-ring` still resolves crypto-bigint 0.5 through jsonwebtoken 11.1's","-p256/p384 dependencies and is affected by","-[RUSTSEC-2026-0387](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0387.html).","-There is no Salvo audit exception for it. Prefer the default AWS-LC JWT backend","-where suitable, audit your application's final lockfile, and see the repository's","-[dependency security policy](../../.github/DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md) for the upstream","-blocker. The alternative configuration below retains this unresolved dependency.","+The JWT dependency is jsonwebtoken 12. Its RustCrypto backend uses the maintained","+p256/p384 0.14 and rsa 0.10 families. Audit your application's final lockfile;","+[the dependency security review](../../.github/DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md) records","+the resolved versions and remaining exceptions in other dependency paths."," "," ```toml"," salvo = { version = \"*\", default-features = false, features = [","@@ -114,12 +110,15 @@ AWS-LC takes precedence when both Salvo JWT provider features are enabled. If"," the application uses a custom process-wide `jsonwebtoken` provider, install"," that provider itself instead of calling `install_crypto_provider`."," ","-The RustCrypto JWT backend currently depends on crypto-bigint affected by","-[RUSTSEC-2026-0387](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0387.html).","-Salvo's middleware uses it for public-key verification. Applications signing","-JWTs with EC private keys should use the default AWS-LC provider until upstream","-dependencies are fixed. See [the dependency security review](../../.github/DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md)","-for the limited audit exception and its review deadline.","+## Upgrading to jsonwebtoken 12","+","+`ConstDecoder::from_secret` now returns `Result<ConstDecoder, JwtError>` and","+rejects empty HMAC secrets. Handle the result with `?` during configuration, or","+use `.expect(\"JWT secret must not be empty\")` for a known nonempty constant.","+The re-exported `DecodingKey::from_secret` and jsonwebtoken's","+`EncodingKey::from_secret` are also fallible. Other constructors keep their","+existing signatures. Direct jsonwebtoken users should upgrade their dependency","+to version 12 so that key types and the process-wide crypto provider match."," "," ## Quick Start"," ","@@ -157,7 +156,7 @@ async fn main() {","     install_crypto_provider()","         .expect(\"install the JWT crypto provider before first use\");"," ","-    let auth = JwtAuth::<Claims, _>::new(ConstDecoder::from_secret(SECRET))","+    let auth = JwtAuth::<Claims, _>::new(ConstDecoder::from_secret(SECRET).expect(\"JWT secret must 